From: OpenIMP campaign
Subject: [PATCH] soc_vpu/helix: ignore residual interrupt status after a finished job

On top of 0099.  Helix can raise a second interrupt for a job whose
ENDFLAG interrupt already completed it (SCH_STAT 0x301 -> 0x100 once the
handler cleared the done flags).  Since 0099 the error branch completed
the wait for it, so the waiter saw no END/BSFULL, reset the core and
dropped a finished picture (~4-6 per hour on a T23).  A status without
ENDFLAG and without an error bit is now ignored; status and length of the
job stay as they are.
---
--- a/drivers/video/soc_vpu/helix/helix.c
+++ b/drivers/video/soc_vpu/helix/helix.c
@@ -612,6 +612,17 @@
 			vpu->status = vpu_stat;
 			complete(&vpu->done);
 
+		} else if (!(vpu_stat & (SCH_STAT_ORESERR | SCH_STAT_BSERR |
+					 SCH_STAT_ACFGERR))) {
+			/*
+			 * No end flag and no error bit: the residue of a
+			 * second invocation for a job whose ENDFLAG interrupt
+			 * already completed it (SCH_STAT 0x301 -> 0x100 once
+			 * the handler cleared the SDE/DBLK done flags).  Keep
+			 * that job's status and length; failing it here (0099)
+			 * dropped a finished picture every few minutes on T23.
+			 */
+			dev_dbg(vpu->vpu.dev, "spurious interrupt, status = %x\n", vpu_stat);
 		} else {
 			check_vpu_status(SCH_STAT_ORESERR, "out fo resolution error!\n");
 			check_vpu_status(SCH_STAT_BSERR, "BS error!\n");
